  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nLight to moderate rain is currently being observed across\ncentral Ohio this morning and will gradually eastward ahead of\na cold front. Scattered to widespread rainfall is expected\nacross the region after dark into early Thursday morning.\nRainfall totals will generally range from a quarter of an inch\nto just shy of inch. Probabilities of localized higher amounts\nbetween 0.50 to 0.75 inches remain elevated (50-65%) across\neastern Ohio, mainly near Zanesville and Coshocton. Despite\nthese higher amounts, the overall threat for flooding remains\nvery low. Rain chances diminish toward daybreak Thursday as mid\nand upper-level dry air advances into the region. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nA deep upper-level low is expected to reach the\nGreat Lakes region Friday. This low should continue eastward \nacross the Upper Ohio Valley region through Saturday.\nTemperatures will likely return to near seasonable levels as\n850mb temperatures drop below freezing. However, the probability\nof snow into next week is considered very low.",
